From: Otto Kekäläinen <otto@debian.org>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 08:36:00 +0000
Subject: Fix IterTreeReducer unpickling when the test runs under pytest

The restricted unpickler added in upstream commit 5a1def7 ("security: add
restricted unpickler to whitelist allowed classes") only allows the
IterTreeReducer test helper classes under the __main__ module. That works when
testing/rorpitertest.py is executed directly, but in Debian CI when autopkgtest
runs, pytest imports it as the module "rorpitertest", causing
TreeReducerTest.testTreeReducerState to fail with:

  _pickle.UnpicklingError: 'rorpitertest.ITRBadder' is neither in the
  allowed whitelist nor a builtin exception

Whitelist the module-qualified test helper classes as well so that the
Debian autopkgtest unit test can run the file through pytest.

Forwarded: https://github.com/rdiff-backup/rdiff-backup/issues/1131
---
 src/rdiffbackup/utils/pickle.py | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/rdiffbackup/utils/pickle.py b/src/rdiffbackup/utils/pickle.py
index b620ce0..fab79c2 100644
--- a/src/rdiffbackup/utils/pickle.py
+++ b/src/rdiffbackup/utils/pickle.py
@@ -79,6 +79,8 @@ class RestrictedUnpickler(_pickle.Unpickler):
         # Required for test.
         "__main__.ITRBadder",
         "__main__.ITRBadder2",
+        "rorpitertest.ITRBadder",
+        "rorpitertest.ITRBadder2",
         "rdiff_backup.rorpiter.IterTreeReducer",
     }
